    "note": [
      "[b]Greenhouse gas emissions[/b]\r\n\r\n[b]How do we measure this?[/b]\r\nNet greenhouse gas emissions as measured by million tonnes carbon dioxide equivalents (MTCO2e).\r\n\r\n[b]Source[/b]\r\n[url=https://www.daera-ni.gov.uk/articles/northern-ireland-greenhouse-gas-inventory]Northern Ireland Greenhouse Gas Inventory[/url], Department of Agriculture, Environment and Rural Affairs\r\n\r\n[b]Impact of Covid-19[/b]\r\nThe decrease from 2022 to 2023, is a continuation of the downward trend from 2022, this is in contrast to the 4% increase in emissions reported for 2021 in the post covid recovery. Emissions in 2023 (20.1 MtCO2e) are now below to those reported in 2020 (21.2 MtCO2e).\r\n\r\n[b]Further Information[/b]\r\n1. Figures are provided in Million tonnes Carbon Dioxide equivalents (MtCO2e).\r\n2. Confidence intervals are only available for the most recent published year of data.\r\n3. UK GHG Base Years are 1990 for carbon dioxide, methane and nitrous oxide; 1995 for fluorinated gases (NF3, HFCs, PFCs and SF6).\r\n4. The NI estimate for the UK GHG Base Year is 26.6 MtCO2e.\r\n5. The entire data series is revised each year.\r\n6. There was a major revision to the GHG inventory in 2019 to better represent peatland emissions. This resulted in an upward shift in overall emissions recorded from 1990-2019 to that previously recorded.\r\n7. Data have been revised to represent GWPs as outlined in IPCC Fifth Assessment Report."
    ],
